<title>FRANCE: Algeria negotiating to buy 150,000 tonnes durum.</title>
<headline>Algeria negotiating to buy 150,000 tonnes durum.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-08-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Algeria is negotiating on Tuesday to buy 150,000 tonnes of optional-origin durum wheat for September and October, grain traders said.</p>
<p>The most likely candidates to supply the durum in a tender include Syria and Canada, they said, noting that European Union durum was out of the loop for the time being.</p>
<p>Algeria bought at least 150,000 tonnes of durum from Syria in late July and unconfirmed reports said it had also bought from Canada, which has been actively promoting sales to the North African country in recent months.</p>
</text>
